    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562">

                <pb facs="0607" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/227: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-17T12:00:00-04:00">October 17,
                            1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>219. If after considering my telegram No. 218, October 16, 9 p.m., you are
                    inclined to grant recognition in the immediate future, please give me
                    preliminary advice of your decision in order that I may send you a final opinion
                    on the political situation. Some people feel that this is a very critical week
                    for the present regime and for this reason it may be well to await developments
                    and withhold a definite decision until the first of next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
